package web

// helpIcon is the reusable contextual-help component (TASK-031, SYS-115,
// UC-037): a "?" trigger button next to a field's label that reveals a
// short localized explanation on pointer hover, keyboard focus, and
// click/tap (never hover-only — SYS-113), with the WCAG 2.2 SC 1.4.13
// behaviors (Escape-dismissible without moving focus, hoverable,
// persistent) driven by the static /static/help.js island — the CSP
// (middleware.go) forbids inline scripts.
//
// Assistive-technology association (UC-037 #4): the trigger is a real
// <button> (keyboard-focusable, accessible name from help.trigger_label)
// and references the popup content via aria-describedby, per the W3C APG
// tooltip pattern — a screen reader announces the help text as the
// trigger's description on focus, whether or not the popup is visually
// open (hidden elements referenced by aria-describedby still contribute
// to the accessible description per the AccName computation). The popup
// carries role="tooltip" and aria-expanded on the trigger tracks the
// visual state for the click/tap "toggletip" mode. The field's own hard
// constraints stay in permanently visible `.hint` text associated with
// the input via ITS aria-describedby (SYS-115: required information never
// lives only inside the popup), so the input-side description channel is
// not overloaded with supplementary prose.
//
// Placement convention (load-bearing for the UC-037 #1 coverage test):
// render @helpIcon immediately AFTER the closing </label> of the field it
// explains — never inside the label (a button inside a label garbles the
// label's accessible name and its click-forwarding). help_test.go
// mechanically pairs each rendered icon with the nearest preceding
// non-hidden input/select in document order and checks the pair against
// the registry (help.go).
//
// key must be a helpRegistry Key; the popup text is the "help.<key>"
// catalog entry (DE/FR complete, SYS-110).
templ helpIcon(p PageData, key string) {
	<span class="help" data-help-key={ key }>
		<button
			type="button"
			class="help-trigger"
			aria-expanded="false"
			aria-describedby={ helpContentID(key) }
			aria-label={ p.T("help.trigger_label") }
		>?</button>
		<span role="tooltip" id={ helpContentID(key) } class="help-popup" hidden>
			{ p.T(helpTextKey(key)) }
		</span>
	</span>
}
